message.content:
This is a men's jacket with an outer shell of cellular polyurethane plastic sheeting backed with woven polyester used only for reinforcement. Under Chapter 59 Note 1 and Note 2, a textile fabric coated or laminated with cellular plastics is classified in 5903 only if the textile is more than mere reinforcement. Here the textile is present only for reinforcement, so the shell material is plastic sheeting of Chapter 39. That makes the garment an article of plastics, which falls in heading 3926 (3926.20 for articles of apparel and clothing accessories, including gloves, made from plastics sheeting).

CBP rulings on similar polyurethane-shell jackets with a textile backing for reinforcement classify them in 3926.20.9050, "Other: Other: Other: Other" (the apparel subheading for other articles of apparel). The 3926.20.90 line has statistical suffixes, and I recall 3926.20.9050 as the one for other apparel, though I am not certain of that suffix.

{"hts_code": "3926.20.9050", "reason": "The jacket's shell is cellular polyurethane plastic sheeting with the woven polyester backing serving only as reinforcement, so it is an article of apparel of plastics under heading 3926 rather than a coated textile garment."}
